DO NOT EDIT these files. They are copies, not AMP source: the whole point of
carrying them is that a config written for upstream Alertmanager renders
byte-identically here. Any AMP-specific template must be added as a separate
file, and users override definitions via the `templates:` config globs (later
definitions win — see FromGlobs in ../template.go).

Re-syncing to a newer upstream release means re-copying both files and
re-generating the golden expectations in ../golden_test.go (its header
documents the generator).
